        "original_id": "40d9aa9a-8a59-522f-9313-a0e40e52aaa9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Géza von Cziffra, Henry Selick, Angelika Hauff, Rudolf Prack, Hermann Erhardt\n- Works: The Queen of the Landstrasse, Moongirl, The Nightmare Before Christmas, James and the Giant Peach, Coraline\n- Music Groups: They Might Be Giants\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, producer, writer, stop motion director\n\nFacts:\n- Géza von Cziffra was a Hungarian and Austrian film director and screenwriter who lived from 19 December 1900 to 28 April 1989.\n- The Queen of the Landstrasse is a 1948 Austrian romance film directed by Géza von Cziffra and starring Angelika Hauff, Rudolf Prack, and Hermann Erhardt.\n- Henry Selick was born on November 30, 1952 and is an American stop motion director, producer, and writer.\n- Henry Selick is best known for directing The Nightmare Before Christmas, James and the Giant Peach, and Coraline.\n- Moongirl was written and directed by Henry Selick.\n- Moongirl features a score by They Might Be Giants.",
